Classify the customer tweet below.

INTENTS (choose exactly one):
- technical_issue: Something in the product malfunctions for this user: app crashes, songs won't play or skip, sound problems, gets logged out, downloads disappear, error codes, features not working, or connection problems with a device (Google Home, Sonos, car, PS4, Apple Watch, Bluetooth).
- service_outage: User suspects a platform-wide outage right now ("is Spotify down?", "not just me", "what's going on with the app"), typically sudden and with no personal detail.
- account_access: Cannot get into the account or the account is compromised: login failures, password reset, email changed without consent, hacked, locked out, wrong Facebook link, unknown email, wants account blocked.
- billing_subscription: Money or plan problems: unexpected or double charges, charged after cancelling, refund requests, Premium not active after paying, student / family / trial / intro-offer eligibility or failures, discount questions, changing country or payment method.
- content_availability: Requests about the music catalogue: add or bring back a song/album/artist, why a track was removed, region-locked content, release timing, explicit versions, wrong metadata, podcast availability.
- feature_feedback: Opinions and suggestions about how the product is designed rather than a malfunction: new feature ideas, UI complaints, shuffle / recommendation quality, ads complaints, praise or criticism of playlists.
- general_question: Informational questions answerable without touching the account: how a feature works, limits (e.g. 3,333 downloads), when Spotify launches in a country, artist / creator tooling, what a promo is, where to find stats.
- other: Not a support request or not workable as one: non-English messages, thanks / praise only, jokes and chit-chat, follow-ups about an existing DM, spam, or messages too vague to classify ("what have you done").

Also decide:
- language: "en" if the tweet is written in English, otherwise the ISO-639-1 code (e.g. "id", "es", "tl").
- needs_account_action: true only if resolving this requires looking up, verifying, or changing THIS user's account, subscription, payment, or saved data (wrong charge, Premium not active, cannot log in, family invite failing, recover a deleted playlist). false if public information or generic troubleshooting steps are enough.
- risk: "none", "security" (hacked / unauthorised access / fraud), "legal" (threatens to sue or involve lawyers), "churn" (threatens to cancel or switch to a competitor, or abuses the support team), "sensitive" (bereavement, health, distress), "wants_human" (asks for a human, says support ignored them, or refers to an existing DM).
- confidence: 0 to 1 for the intent.
- summary: one short sentence describing the problem.

Tie-breaks: a question about how to do something, or whether it is possible today, is general_question even if the answer is 'not possible'; feature_feedback is a suggestion or a complaint about the design. A trial, plan or Premium status that looks wrong for THIS user needs_account_action=true. Cannot log in / lost access to the account email / hacked is account_access even if money is mentioned.

Examples:
Tweet: "my downloads keep vanishing every week on android, so annoying" -> {"intent": "technical_issue", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Offline downloads are repeatedly removed on Android."}
Tweet: "is spotify down?? nothing loads for me or my friends" -> {"intent": "service_outage", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Suspects a platform-wide outage."}
Tweet: "someone changed my email and now I'm locked out of my account" -> {"intent": "account_access", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": true, "risk": "security", "confidence": 0.95, "summary": "Account taken over; email changed; locked out."}
Tweet: "you charged me twice this month, I want my money back" -> {"intent": "billing_subscription", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": true, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.95, "summary": "Double charge, refund requested."}
Tweet: "when does the 3 months for $0.99 offer end?" -> {"intent": "billing_subscription", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.85, "summary": "Asks about intro offer end date (public information)."}
Tweet: "please add the new drake album already!!" -> {"intent": "content_availability", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Wants an album added to the catalogue."}
Tweet: "shuffle is so bad, it plays the same 20 songs out of 500" -> {"intent": "feature_feedback", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.85, "summary": "Complaint about shuffle design."}
Tweet: "how many songs can I download for offline?" -> {"intent": "general_question", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Asks about the offline download limit."}
Tweet: "thanks for the help yesterday, you guys rock" -> {"intent": "other", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Thanks only."}
Tweet: "app crashes every day, I'm switching to apple music if this isn't fixed" -> {"intent": "technical_issue", "language": "en", "needs_account_action": false, "risk": "churn", "confidence": 0.9, "summary": "Daily crashes; threatens to switch to a competitor."}
Tweet: "no puedo iniciar sesión en mi cuenta premium" -> {"intent": "account_access", "language": "es", "needs_account_action": true, "risk": "none", "confidence": 0.85, "summary": "Cannot log in (Spanish)."}
